Feature: slice-4 / admin-user-crud
Branch: feat/web-app-slice-4-cont
Verified: 2026-05-28
Anchored to: docs/18 §13.8 (AdminUpdateUser + AdminDeleteUser forms)

What was built
==============
- /admin/users route — global user list (server shell at
  src/app/[locale]/admin/users/page.tsx).
- src/components/admin/UsersList.tsx — client component:
  * Calls identityClient.adminListUsers with pageSize=25 + 300ms
    search debounce + role filter dropdown.
  * 5-column table: name (first+last), email, role (localized
    label), organization_id (truncated), inline Edit/Delete actions.
  * Cursor-based pagination via next_page_token + page-stack walk
    (same pattern as OrgsList).
  * UserEditDialog — inline ActionDialog with the high-frequency
    edit fields per §13.8: first_name, last_name, email, phone_
    number, role, ui_language. Delta-only submit (only changed
    fields sent), "noChange" guard if user only filled the reason.
  * UserDeleteDialog — soft-delete via AdminDeleteUser, single
    reason field, dialog body shows the user's display name +
    email so the operator confirms the right row.
  * Tolerant enum handling — Connect-Web JSON ships UserRole as
    proto names, proto-es types it as numeric; cast through
    unknown both ways (same trick as the OrgsList enum coercion +
    AdminGuard role check).

i18n: messages/{pl,en}.json grow with admin.users.* — title,
subhead, searchPlaceholder, roleFilterAll, loading/empty/error,
column headers, edit/delete buttons + dialog titles/bodies,
form-field labels, noChange guard, role label mapping for all
five UserRole values.

How verified
============
1. `pnpm build` exit 0. Route table now includes:
     /[locale]/admin/users    ● SSG (×2 locales)

2. HTTP smoke:
     /admin/users    → 200
     /en/admin/users → 200

3. Puppeteer screenshots:
     users-gate-pl-full.png — Polish AdminGuard sign-in panel on
       /admin/users. Confirms the route is reachable and the
       AdminGuard fires before any RPC.
     users-gate-en-full.png — same in English.

4. preview_console_logs(error) returns "No console logs". The
   guard's getMyProfile catch swallows the unauthed RPC failure
   silently.

Compliance with docs/18 §13.8
=============================
- ✓ Search by name or email (backend's `search` param is ILIKE).
- ✓ Filter by role.
- ✓ Pagination.
- ✓ Edit user — high-frequency fields: name, email, phone, role,
  ui_language.
- ✓ Delete user — soft-delete via AdminDeleteUser with reason.
- ☐ Deferred fields on edit (separate sub-feature when needed):
  organization_id transfer, default_modality_id, timezone,
  professional_title, credentials_number, biography, avatar_url,
  billing_address. AdminUpdateUserRequest has all of them as
  `optional`, so adding fields to the dialog is incremental work
  that doesn't change the wire contract.

Live screenshot of the populated table requires an authenticated
SUPERWIZOR_ADMIN session with seeded user data — same constraint
as the rest of the admin features. Code path verified by build +
type-check against the proto-es schemas.

